kwin_x11: build screens from RandR monitors, and follow their changes

kwin_x11 makes one screen per CRTC that drives a connected output and never
asks for the RandR 1.5 monitors, which are what Xinerama and the toolkits
report. On a server whose one framebuffer a client splits into monitors — a
streamed desktop, where Selkies publishes one monitor per display over the
single output a framebuffer server has — every screen of kwin's therefore spans
the whole framebuffer, and a maximized window covers every display at once.

Screens are now the monitors wherever the server reports any, each keeping the
CRTC, rotation, refresh rate and EDID of its first driven output; a server that
defines no monitors reports one per active output, so real hardware is
unchanged, and a server without RandR 1.5 takes the CRTC path as before.
Selkies announces a monitor change through an output property, since
RRSetMonitor emits no event of its own, so output property notifications are
selected and re-read the outputs the way a screen change does.

Applies to kwin-x11 6.6.x (verified against 6.6.4).

